----------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT THE WEB SOURCE IS (parity scope)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
`AISuggestNewGeofences.tsx` is an `useAiStream` + `AIFeatureCard` + `withAiFeature` panel
(NOT a chart/map card). It:
  • streams POST /ai/geofences/draft (location_id in the JSON body, no path param);
  • captures a typed `tool_result` whose name === 'draft_geofence' && ok === true, unwraps
    the NESTED envelope `data.draft.{location_id,vehicle_id,proposed_name,radius_m,
    centroid_lat,centroid_lon}` + wrapper `status` ('ok'|'invalid'|str) + optional wrapper
    `validation_error`, narrowing every field with `typeof` guards (drops a partial frame);
  • renders the proposal box (Proposed geofence label + name + "Radius: {round} m" +
    validation_error + a "rejected by validator" line when status != 'ok') with an
    "Apply to form" button DISABLED unless status === 'ok' (computed, never literal);
  • on Apply forwards {name, latitude(centroid_lat), longitude(centroid_lon), radius(radius_m)}
    to the parent — the AI panel NEVER writes the API; the baseline Add Geofence Save is the
    sole write path;
  • cancels + clears the draft on locationId change and unmount;
  • is wrapped by `withAiFeature('suggest-new-geofences')` → ABSENT (null) when AI is off.

